A.aDS=s(["Two observations per line, and only two: the date it finished, or a tick that it had not finished one week after the festival day. This is not a stocktake \u2014 tyohari does not measure how much was left or what it was worth.","A run-out date is only as good as the day someone noticed. If nobody wrote it down that evening, leave the line blank \u2014 a blank line is honest, a guessed date is not. Blank lines show as \u2014 and are excluded from every count, and the count says how many were recorded.",'The tick is not dated by you. It means "had not finished as of one week after the festival day", whenever you actually ticked it.',"@@TWO_COLUMNS@@","The year columns are a RECORD, not a recommendation. The quantity column is deliberately blank. tyohari suggests nothing, predicts nothing and ranks nothing.","tyohari does not know when any festival is. You typed the name and the date, and it does not adjust for the festival moving between years \u2014 the columns sit side by side and you read them yourself.","Cost is what your wholesaler billed you, exactly as you typed it. There is no selling price, no margin, no GST and no profit anywhere in this app.","Freight and hamali are split across lines by cost (or equally, your choice) using largest-remainder rounding: the parts always sum to the exact rupee you entered, though one line may differ by a paisa from cost \xd7 ratio.","The unit rate beside each line is display only. It is never multiplied back into a cost, so its rounding cannot leak into your totals.",'Items are matched across years by name. "Ghee (Gold Tin)" and "Gold Tin Ghee" are NOT matched automatically \u2014 tap "same as last year\u2019s ___" once and tyohari remembers.'],t.s)
